   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAOln0",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I am asking you to give your party vote to ACT. I want more ACT MPs who will fight to cut waste and grow the country, balance the books with no new taxes, defend equal rights, deliver better public services, cut red tape, and restore real consequences for crime. I'm asking you to choose whichever electorate candidate you believe will best represent the North Shore electorate and to give your party vote to ACT."
     },
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAOlpq",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I'm asking you to give your party vote to ACT to Lock Labour Out and unlock New Zealand's potential. It means keeping the coalition Government in power, but ensuring that it can go further and faster on the issues that matter most to you. A party vote for ACT will re-elect the Government and make it stronger. I am currently the Minister for Children and Minister for the Prevention of Family Violence and Sexual Violence."
     },
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAOlsg",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Continue to tackle youth crime while also improving the safety and wellbeing of children in care."
     },
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAOlvW",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Grow the economy to balance the books with no new taxes so incomes rise faster than living costs."
     },
     {
      "_key": "MBeO7ojrohBwl7F7zAOlyM",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Deliver better services for taxpayers: education, police, and match Australia on medicines funding."
     }
    ],
